// Lowering rules for GOARCH=ppc (32-bit PowerPC, the scalar G3 baseline).
//
// The 64-bit operations are not lowered here. The generic dec64 decomposition
// (decompose.go / _gen/dec64.rules) has already turned every 64-bit value into a
// (hi, lo) pair of 32-bit values before this file runs, including the arithmetic
// for Add64/Sub64/Mul64/shifts and the big-endian load and store split, so the
// rules below only have to give the 32-bit residue a machine form.
//
// The carry is the part that is not mechanical. XER[CA] is a single machine bit
// that the pair (addc, adde) shares through, and no instruction can read or write
// it directly, so:
//
//   - Add32carry becomes ADDC, whose second result is the carry as an SSA value
//     of type Flags;
//   - Add32withcarry takes that Flags value as an explicit third argument and
//     becomes ADDE. The Flags argument is a real data dependence, so a scheduler
//     cannot move an unrelated instruction between the addc and the adde; and
//   - every op that writes CA is marked clobberFlags in _gen/PPCOps.go, so the
//     flag allocator treats a carry as destroyed by an instruction that does not
//     produce it, and recomputes it (flagalloc's copyFlags) if one lands in
//     between. That is the whole XER[CA] model; DESIGN.md §5 names addic, srawi,
//     sraw, the subfc family and adde as the clobbering forms.

// Lowering arithmetic.
(Add32 x y) => (ADD x y)
(Add32carry x y) => (ADDC x y)
(Add32withcarry x y c) => (ADDE x y c)
(Add32carrywithcarry x y c) => (ADDEC x y c)
(Sub32 x y) => (SUB x y)
(Sub32carry x y) => (SUBC x y)
(Sub32withcarry x y c) => (SUBE x y c)
(Mul32 x y) => (MULLW x y)
(Mul32uhilo x y) => (MULLU x y)
(And32 x y) => (AND x y)
(Or32 x y) => (OR x y)
(Xor32 x y) => (XOR x y)
(Neg32 x) => (NEG x)

// Lowering shifts. slw and srw take the low six bits of the count and return
// zero when bit 5 is set, which is the same answer Go specifies for a shift of 32
// or more on a 32-bit type, so no extra count check is needed here.
(Lsh32x32 x y) => (SLW x y)
(Lsh32x64 x y) => (SLW x y)
(Rsh32Ux32 x y) => (SRW x y)
(Rsh32Ux64 x y) => (SRW x y)
(Rsh32x32 x y) => (SRAW x y)
(Rsh32x64 x y) => (SRAW x y)

// Lowering addresses, loads and stores. A 64-bit load or store has already been
// split into two big-endian 32-bit accesses by _gen/dec64.rules, so every case
// here is at most register width.
(OffPtr [off] ptr) => (MOVWaddr [int32(off)] ptr)
(Addr {sym} base) => (MOVWaddr {sym} base)
(LocalAddr <t> {sym} base mem) && t.Elem().HasPointers() => (MOVWaddr {sym} (SPanchored base mem))
(LocalAddr <t> {sym} base _) && !t.Elem().HasPointers() => (MOVWaddr {sym} base)

(Load <t> ptr mem) && t.IsBoolean() => (MOVBUload ptr mem)
(Load <t> ptr mem) && is8BitInt(t) && t.IsSigned() => (MOVBload ptr mem)
(Load <t> ptr mem) && is8BitInt(t) && !t.IsSigned() => (MOVBUload ptr mem)
(Load <t> ptr mem) && is16BitInt(t) && t.IsSigned() => (MOVHload ptr mem)
(Load <t> ptr mem) && is16BitInt(t) && !t.IsSigned() => (MOVHUload ptr mem)
(Load <t> ptr mem) && (is32BitInt(t) || isPtr(t)) => (MOVWload ptr mem)

(Store {t} ptr val mem) && t.Size() == 1 => (MOVBstore ptr val mem)
(Store {t} ptr val mem) && t.Size() == 2 => (MOVHstore ptr val mem)
(Store {t} ptr val mem) && t.Size() == 4 && !t.IsFloat() => (MOVWstore ptr val mem)

// Lowering constants and register moves.
(Const32 [c]) => (MOVWconst [c])
(ConstBool [t]) => (MOVWconst [b2i32(t)])
(ConstNil) => (MOVWconst [0])
(Copy x) => (MOVWreg x)
